thread:
Lina: Noticed a confusing pair of snippets in the Node quickstart: one uses async/await and the other uses callback-style thenables. New devs are confused which is recommended. Also the README shows `REDWOOD_KEY` in one spot and `REDWOOD_API_KEY` in another.
Omar: Can you paste the exact locations?
Lina: Quickstarts/node-chat/README.md lines 12-30. It has two snippets:
```javascript
// snippet A (async)
const Redwood = require('@redwood/inference')
const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.REDWOOD_API_KEY })
async function run(){
  const r = await client.generate({ model: 'redwood-1', prompt: 'hi' })
  console.log(r.text)
}
run()
```
and later:
```javascript
// snippet B (then)
const { RedwoodClient } = require('@redwood/inference')
const client = new RedwoodClient({ apiKey: process.env.REDWOOD_KEY })
client.generate({ model: 'redwood-1', prompt: 'hi' }).then(res => console.log(res.text))
```
Lina: So drift: env var name mismatch and different import styles and different async patterns.
Maya: Yikes. That explains the new contributor confusion I saw in onboarding channel.
ci-bot: :robot_face: docs-linter found 3 issues in /quickstarts/node-chat/README.md: inconsistent env var, deprecated named import, and mixed async styles. See https://ci.internal.redwood/docs-lint/4622
Omar: We should standardize to one canonical snippet style (async/await) and prefer the default export per Node SDK v1.2+. Also update all env var references to REDWOOD_API_KEY.
Theo: Agreed. I'll open a PR to normalize the snippets and add a short note about sync vs async choices. Also propose a tiny docs-lint rule to flag multiple snippet styles in the same README.
Maya: Can we also add an example showing a simple retry wrapper for transient errors? Many examples assume instant success and newcomers hit 502s. A short snippet like:
```javascript
// minimal retry helper
async function withRetries(fn, attempts=3){
  for(let i=0;i<attempts;i++){
    try{ return await fn() }catch(e){ if(i===attempts-1) throw e; await new Promise(r=>setTimeout(r, 100*(2**i))) }
  }
}

await withRetries(()=>client.generate({ model:'redwood-1', prompt:'hi' }))
```
Omar: Good idea. We have SDK-level retries but examples should surface both default behavior and how to customize.
Lina: I opened PR 1569: https://github.com/redwood-inference/examples/pull/1569 which: (1) standardizes to async/await snippets with default export import, (2) replaces REDWOOD_KEY with REDWOOD_API_KEY everywhere, (3) adds the minimal retry helper and a short note about SDK defaults.
ci-bot: :white_check_mark: PR 1569 passed docs-lint and the new quickstart smoke CI (node index.js against mock server).
Theo: Thanks. Follow-ups: add a docs-site migration note for examples mentioning the preferred snippet style, add the docs-lint rule, and audit other quickstarts for similar inconsistencies. I'll assign myself and Maya.
Maya: I'll scan Python and Go quickstarts for equivalent drift (imports, env vars, sync/async semantics).
Lina: Once merged I'll ping onboarding and community channels so educators can update materials.
Omar: Awesome work, team. This should reduce first-week confusion a lot. :tada:
